    "id": "arena:48748656",
    "source": "arena",
    "type": "block",
    "title": "savannah brown - \"on the fear\"",
    "text": "as a kid I’d get a new journal every so often and decide this journal to be the one. perfect! pristine! it would contain only beautiful thoughts in my tidiest handwriting and every page would be full. naturally this never happened. if I spelled a word wrong in pen, whatever, I’d get frustrated and ditch the whole notebook. wasteful little wench. obviously here the notebook is your body of work and, in a real way, your one, unditachable life. you don’t get another and you will mess up and still you must go again. you simply cannot let yourself be so paralyzed by fear that you don’t even interact with the blankness. now when I get a new notebook – this is completely true – I intentionally fuck it up, write something sloppy, spill coffee on it, tear pages out unprecisely. and too will your work live like this.\n\nfrom member's only patreon post, Monday October 16th 2023",
    "url": "https://www.are.na/block/24185556",
    "published_at": "2023-10-16T14:31:44.000Z",
